  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/3f1f1f7b-5592-42fa-9613-e2c0eb2f217a.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 142px;\" /><br />Slope of <math><mi>S</mi><mi>F</mi></math> is <math><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Slope of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math><br />Now, the slope of <math><mi>E</mi><mi>S</mi></math> is <math><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> Slope of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />Equation of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Equation of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> is <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />Hence, point <math><mi>A</mi></math> is <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
